# Gitignored paths a new worktree needs to be immediately usable.
# `wt step copy-ignored` copies a path only if it is BOTH gitignored AND
# matched here.
#
# NOTE: patterns match the entries git reports as ignored, and git reports a
# wholesale-ignored directory as the directory itself. A pattern naming a file
# *inside* such a directory matches nothing, and `[step.copy-ignored] exclude`
# cannot subtract from within one either — it is all-or-nothing per entry. So
# keep .gitignore precise; anything needed out of a coarsely-ignored directory
# needs its own copy hook in .config/wt.toml.
#
# Deliberately absent:
#   .codegraph/       rebuilt by the `graph` post-start hook
#   buildServer.json  rebuilt by the `lsp` post-start hook (it hardcodes
#                     absolute paths to whichever checkout generated it)

.claude/settings.local.json
.vscode/
